# target: one shell pattern a line, in C names (the object format's prefix
# taken off, as the build records it in runtime/symbol-prefix). What a
# target allows besides is in NAME/allowed, NAME one of the names the host
# answers to (linux, macos), as the runner names an expected.NAME.
